2. Pure-OSI Boundary (0 BSL-1.1) & NocoBase 2.2.50 Clause 5.2 Attribution
================================================================================
CTU-OpenPaw enforces a strict Pure-OSI source repository policy (0 BSL-1.1 /
Business Source License software across source code, workspace dependencies,
SBOM components, and core infrastructure).

- LatticeDX source repositories contain ZERO upstream/nocobase Git submodules,
  ZERO .gitmodules files, and do not copy, embed, or redistribute NocoBase
  upstream source code.
- Host NocoBase runtime (nocobase/nocobase:2.2.50@sha256:04b75164936e7314ef74d82844bc56c9f34ed7ff1ca976ca53ffac2d3c88d777)
  is executed strictly as an external OCI container outside the Git repositories.
- All 7 first-party LatticeDX NocoBase plugins declare
  "nocobase": { "sdkProvidedByHost": true }, invoke host SDK APIs at runtime,
  and transparently preserve NocoBase License Agreement (updated 2026-02-24)
  Clause 5.2 UI attribution:
    * "Powered by NocoBase"
    * Version: "v2.2.50"
    * Link: https://www.nocobase.com
    * "License settings"

